{# A community's sidebar - the identity card (with the manage stub
   action at the bottom of that same card - see community_sidebar_header's
   own comment for why it stays there while join/leave and "write a
   post" don't), then the membership (join/leave) card, then a read-only
   aggregate rating across the community's own posts, basic stats, and
   the members list - in that order, matching profile-sidebar.twig +
   show.twig's own rating -> stats -> friends order for a personal
   profile. The membership card sits right after the header, in the same
   relative position profile-sidebar.twig's own profile_info ("About the
   user") card occupies right after profile_card - relationshipStatus
   there is a genuinely separate concern from the identity card, same as
   here. Originally inline in community-show.twig's own
   sidebar_widgets block; extracted here so community.post-show
   (UsersController::showCommunityPostPage(), template blog-post.show.twig)
   can show the same community sidebar a post's parent community page
   does, instead of the post author's profile-sidebar.twig - a post inside
   a community is more "part of the community" than "part of the author's
   personal blog", same reasoning community.show already reflects.

   Included with `only` from every caller (see both callers' own comments)
   so its bare `relationshipStatus` here can never pick up an unrelated
   ambient value of the same name from the includer's own scope (e.g.
   blog-post.show.twig already has its own `relationshipStatus` for the
   friend-request button - a different domain than this partial's
   community-scoped one).

   Expected variables: community (Feed), imageUrl (string - community's
   own imageUrl or CommunityService::DEFAULT_IMAGE_URL, already resolved
   by the controller via CommunityService::resolveImageUrl() - see that
   method's own docblock for why this isn't a method on Feed itself),
   owner (User|null), ownerUrl
   (string|null), relationshipStatus (string: owner/moderator/member/
   pending/none - CommunityService::getRelationshipStatus()),
   membershipActionUrl (string), members
   (list), hasMembers (bool), membersTotal (int), membersApiUrl
   (string), membersNextOffset (int|null), ratingCount (int),
   ratingAverage (float|null), ratingFullStars (int), ratingHasHalfStar
   (bool), ratingHint (string|null) - the aggregate across this
   community's own posts (UsersController::buildCommunityRatingViewData()),
   NOT a vote on the community feed itself - postCount (int, posts
   parented under this community), commentCount (int, comments left on
   those posts) and createdAtLabel (string|null -
   UsersController::buildCommunityStatsViewData()). #}

{% block community_sidebar_header %}
    {# Community identity card - avatar/title/creator/description, plus
       the manage stub action at the bottom of this same card rather than
       as a separate card below it - same layout profile-sidebar.twig's
       profile_card already uses for "Edit profile". The
       join/leave membership action does NOT live here - see
       community_membership below for why - and "write a post" moved to
       community-show.twig's own feed header ("New post", next to the
       feed it adds to) instead of a sidebar stub, mirroring where
       show.twig puts the equivalent button for a personal blog. Used to
       live at the top of community-show.twig's own content column; moved
       to the top of this shared sidebar so community.post-show (a single
       post's page) shows the same "which community is this" context a
       post's own community.show page does. #}
    <div class="card mb-3">
        <div class="card-body">
            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-3">
                <img
                    src="{{ imageUrl }}"
                    alt="{{ community.title }}"
                    class="rounded-circle border bg-body-secondary object-fit-cover flex-shrink-0"
                    width="80"
                    height="80"
                >
                <div class="flex-grow-1">
                    <h2 class="h5 mb-1">{{ community.title }}</h2>
                    {% if owner %}
                        <p class="text-body-secondary small mb-0">
                            {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.01') }}
                            {% if ownerUrl %}
                                <a href="{{ ownerUrl }}" class="text-body">{{ owner.getDisplayName() }}</a>
                            {% else %}
                                {{ owner.getDisplayName() }}
                            {% endif %}
                        </p>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </div>

            {% if community.description %}
                <p class="card-text mt-3 mb-0">{{ community.description }}</p>
            {% endif %}

            {% block community_manage_stub %}
                {# "Manage" - links to action=community.manage (see
                   UsersController::showCommunityManagePage()). Owner-only
                   (manageUrl is only ever set for the community's own
                   owner - see showCommunityShowPage()) - a moderator no
                   longer sees this button at all, now that it actually
                   goes somewhere real rather than being a shared disabled
                   stub (per this feature's own spec, "Owner access
                   only"). #}
                {% if manageUrl %}
                    <div class="d-grid gap-2 mt-3">
                        <a href="{{ manageUrl }}" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
                            <i class="bi bi-gear me-1"></i>{{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.02') }}
                        </a>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            {% endblock %}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block community_membership %}
    {# The join/leave action, as its own card right after the header -
       same relative position profile-sidebar.twig's profile_info ("About
       the user") occupies right after profile_card. Unlike
       community_manage_stub (which really is just a secondary action
       bolted onto the identity card), a viewer's own membership status
       is a distinct, standalone fact about them and this community,
       worth its own card rather than being buried at the bottom of the
       identity one.

       data-membership-url/data-status are picked up by users.ts's
       initCommunityMembershipButton() - a click rewrites this button in
       place from the JSON {status} the API responds with, same pattern
       as profile-sidebar.twig's .friend-action-btn/initFriendButton(). #}
    <div class="card mb-3">
        <div class="card-body">
            {% if isGuest %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary w-100" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#authFormModal">
                    <i class="bi bi-person-plus"></i> {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.03') }}
                </button>
            {% elseif relationshipStatus == 'owner' %}
                <p class="card-text text-body-secondary small mb-0">
                    <i class="bi bi-patch-check"></i> {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.04') }}
                </p>
            {% elseif relationshipStatus == 'pending' %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary community-membership-btn w-100" data-membership-url="{{ membershipActionUrl }}" data-action="remove" data-status="pending">
                    <i class="bi bi-hourglass-split"></i> {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.05') }}
                </button>
                <p class="text-body-secondary small mt-2 mb-0">{{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.06') }}</p>
            {% elseif relationshipStatus == 'member' or relationshipStatus == 'moderator' %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary community-membership-btn w-100" data-membership-url="{{ membershipActionUrl }}" data-action="remove" data-status="{{ relationshipStatus }}">
                    <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-right"></i> {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.07') }}
                </button>
            {% elseif relationshipStatus == 'none' %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary community-membership-btn w-100" data-membership-url="{{ membershipActionUrl }}" data-action="add" data-status="none">
                    <i class="bi bi-person-plus"></i> {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.03') }}
                </button>
            {% else %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary w-100" disabled title="{{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.08') }}">
                    <i class="bi bi-person-plus"></i> {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.03') }}
                </button>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block community_rating %}
    {# NOT a vote on the community feed itself - a community (like a
       personal blog) is never something a viewer rates directly, only
       individual posts are rateable (see UsersController::
       buildCommunityRatingViewData()). #}
    {% include 'components/common/rating-card.twig' with {
        count: ratingCount ?? 0,
        average: ratingAverage ?? null,
        fullStars: ratingFullStars ?? 0,
        hasHalfStar: ratingHasHalfStar ?? false,
        hint: ratingHint ?? null,
        emptyText: trans('view.users.community.sidebar.09'),
    } only %}
{% endblock %}

{% block community_stats %}
    {# Same row set as show.twig's profile_stats (posts/comments/date)
       - "Members" was dropped from here since the members list right
       below already shows that count in its own heading; a comment count
       across the community's own posts is the more useful "how active is
       this place" number, matching the profile page's own stats card. #}
    {% set statsRows = [
        {label: trans('view.users.community.sidebar.10'), value: postCount ?? 0},
        {label: trans('view.users.community.sidebar.11'), value: commentCount ?? 0},
    ] %}
    {% if createdAtLabel %}
        {% set statsRows = statsRows|merge([{label: trans('view.users.community.sidebar.12'), value: createdAtLabel}]) %}
    {% endif %}
    {% include 'components/common/stats-card.twig' with {rows: statsRows} only %}
{% endblock %}

{% block community_members %}
    {# data-members-api-url is read by users.ts's
       initCommunityMembersLoadMore() - same "Show more" AJAX-append
       pattern as #friends-list/initFriendsLoadMore() on the profile
       page. Only real members show up here (pending subscribers don't -
       see MembershipRepository::findMembers()'s own docblock). #}
    <div class="card mb-3" id="community-members" data-members-api-url="{{ membersApiUrl }}">
        <div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h6 card-title mb-3">
                {{ trans('community.manage_members') }}
                {% if membersTotal %}<span class="text-body-secondary">({{ membersTotal }})</span>{% endif %}
            </h2>
            {% if hasMembers %}
                <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-2" id="community-members-items">
                    {% for member in members %}
                        {% block community_members_item %}
                            <a href="{{ member.url ?: '#' }}" class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 text-body text-decoration-none">
                                <img src="{{ member.avatarUrl }}" alt="" class="rounded-circle bg-body-secondary object-fit-cover flex-shrink-0" width="36" height="36">
                                <span class="small">{{ member.displayName }}</span>
                                {% if member.roleLabel %}<span class="badge text-bg-secondary ms-auto">{{ member.roleLabel }}</span>{% endif %}
                            </a>
                        {% endblock %}
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
                {% if membersNextOffset is not null %}
                    <div class="text-center mt-2" data-community-members-load-more-wrapper>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm load-more-community-members" data-offset="{{ membersNextOffset }}">
                            {{ trans('view.users.community.sidebar.13') }}
                        </button>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            {% else %}
                <p class="card-text text-body-secondary small mb-0">{{ trans('view.users.community.manage.members.05') }}</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
